{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Pass over to Tarshish.</b> With a heh, like unto Tarshish." "<b>Inhabitants of [the island].</b> Every island."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra explains the suffixed form תרשישה as equivalent in meaning to אל תרשיש, the heh being directional.", 1 "Bracketed text reflects the lemma as cited; Ibn Ezra glosses the singular as collective."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:48.101205769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}